  "question": {
    "text": "A current of 5A exists in a square loop of side $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\mathrm{~m}$. Then the magnitude of the magnetic field $B$ at the centre of the square loop will be $p \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~T}$. where, value of p is _____ .\n$\\left[\\right.$ Take $\\left.\\mu_0=4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{TmA}^{-1}\\right]$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/pySAD5X6_LyAZco4PYXpIM73nvSRgqoU0bOZH0dYkSc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\nLet B be the magnetic field due to single side\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { then } B=\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}{4 \\pi \\mathrm{~d}}\\left(\\sin \\theta_1+\\sin \\theta_2\\right) \\\\\n& =\\frac{10^{-7} \\times 5 \\times 2}{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}} \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=2 \\times 10^{-6} \\\\\n& \\therefore B_{\\text {net }} \\text { at centre } O=4 B \\\\\n& =8 \\times 10^{-6}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
